# Dual remote push (GitHub + GitLab)

When you finish implementing requested code/content changes in this project, **commit and push without waiting for the user to ask**.

## Remotes

| Remote | URL | Branch |
|---|---|---|
| `origin` (GitHub) | `https://github.com/arunsaikumarB/luxury-home-builder.git` | `main` (also update current feature branch if applicable) |
| `gitlab` | `http://gitlab.lstech-hq.lstechinc.com/websites/dh-builders.git` | `dh-builder-v1` |

## Workflow after meaningful changes

1. Stage only relevant project files (never secrets / `.env`).
2. Commit with a clear message (follow repo commit style).
3. Push to **both**:
   - `git push origin HEAD:main` (or current GitHub-tracking branch)
   - `git push gitlab HEAD:dh-builder-v1` (or current GitLab-tracking branch)
4. If on `dh-builder-v1`, push that branch to GitLab and also push/sync `main` to GitHub when the work belongs on both.
5. Report both remote URLs briefly when done.

## Exceptions

- Do **not** push if the user only asked a question / review with no code edits.
- Do **not** force-push unless the user explicitly asks.
- Skip empty commits when there is nothing to commit.
